taris-tipd-dkms

The USB-C controller driver (drivers/usb/typec/tipd) from Asahi Linux's kernel source
(https://github.com/AsahiLinux/linux), by its authors and the Asahi Linux contributors. The
package holds no kernel source: asahi-source.sh fetches the driver's source for each kernel it's
built for. Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 (some files version 2 or
later, as their SPDX lines say).

Changed by TarisOS (https://github.com/TarisOS/tarisOS) in 2026, by applying two commits by Janne
Grunau from Asahi Linux's work-in-progress branches, so the display driver is told when a display
on USB-C comes and goes:

- 0001-usb-typec-tipd-Track-data_status-changes-for-CD321x.patch
- 0002-usb-typec-tipd-HACK-Use-drm-oob-hotplug-event.patch

core.c and tps6598x.h, the files they change, say so near their tops (taris-notices.patch). The
patches are in TarisOS's source, packaging/pkgbuilds/taris-tipd-dkms.
